  <prompt>Build useRecordHeaderToolbarActions hook at src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/useRecordHeaderToolbarActions.ts per FR-07/08/08a/09/10/11 (REVISED post task 001). Signature: useRecordHeaderToolbarActions({ entity, recordId, recordSummary }) — accepts recordSummary as an OPTIONAL string prop passed by the consumer (from useRecordFieldValues). Returns fully-formed IHeaderToolbarProps with 3 wired slots. **Sparkle** opens Fluent v9 popover showing the recordSummary string inline (or empty state if null/empty) + refresh icon rendered UNWIRED in R1 (tooltip: "Refresh available in a follow-on release"). NO separate Xrm.WebApi call for the summary — sprk_recordsummary is a MULTILINE TEXT field already fetched by the consumer per FR-12. **Checkmark** opens SmartTodo Layout 1 (85%x85%); badge from useRelatedCount('sprk_todo', `_regardingobjectid_value eq ${recordId}`). **Annotation** opens Notepad (70%x80%); badge from useRelatedCount('sprk_memo', entity-specific-lookup filter for the current entity per SUPPORTED_MEMO_PARENTS map from toolbarLaunchDefaults). If entity is NOT in SUPPORTED_MEMO_PARENTS, memo badge is 0 (Notepad will show an error on click). **See notes/design-alignment-corrections.md.**</prompt>

  <role>Spaarke platform developer. React hooks + Fluent v9 Popover expert; Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo experienced.</role>

  <goal>useRecordHeaderToolbarActions.ts + unit tests; three slots emitted with correct handlers; sparkle uses Popover (no navigateTo); refresh icon UNWIRED; enabled flags respected.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design §3.4 with spec FR-08 revised: sparkle click opens a Fluent v9 popover (not modal) with sprk_recordsummary body + refresh icon (unwired in R1 per FR-08a — deferred to a follow-on BFF project). This is the LINCHPIN hook that per-entity PCFs consume without re-implementing toolbar wiring.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/useRecordHeaderToolbarActions.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/__tests__/useRecordHeaderToolbarActions.test.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/HeaderToolbar/types.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-07: IUseRecordHeaderToolbarActionsOptions { entity; recordId; enabled?: { sparkle?; checkmark?; annotation?; } }. Enabled defaults all true.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-08 REVISED: sparkle opens Fluent v9 popover with summary body (no navigateTo).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-08a NEW: refresh icon rendered but NOT wired in R1 — click is no-op with tooltip stating deferral.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-09: checkmark opens SmartTodo webresource at 85%x85%.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-10: annotation opens Notepad webresource at 70%x80%.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-11: badges refresh on mount + window-focus.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">NFR-07: zero new BFF endpoints; refresh icon MUST stay unwired.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Xrm.WebApi only; no BFF.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/record-header-and-notepad-r1/spec.md</file>
