  <justification>
    <existing>None. Per-entity toolbar wiring does not exist as a shared hook.</existing>
    <extension>N/A — this is the extraction point.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every per-entity PCF (MatterHeaderPcf now; ProjectHeaderPcf, InvoiceHeaderPcf next) would re-implement the same three-action wiring, then diverge over time. §11 anti-pattern.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Declare IUseRecordHeaderToolbarActionsOptions { entity: string; recordId: string; recordSummary?: string | null; enabled?: {...}; } and return type IHeaderToolbarProps.</step>
    <step order="2">Fetch memo count via useRelatedCount("sprk_memo", buildMemoFilter(entity, recordId)) where buildMemoFilter uses SUPPORTED_MEMO_PARENTS[entity] to construct `_${lookup-field}_value eq ${recordId}` (returns null if entity unsupported → memo badge 0). Fetch todo count via useRelatedCount("sprk_todo", `_regardingobjectid_value eq ${recordId}`).</step>
    <step order="3">**Removed** per task 001 correction — sprk_recordsummary is NOT a separate entity; the consumer passes the value in via recordSummary prop from useRecordFieldValues.</step>
    <step order="4">Build sparkle slot: onClick opens a Fluent v9 Popover anchored to the sparkle button (use useState for open/closed). Popover content: options.recordSummary body if non-empty; else empty-state "No summary yet"; refresh icon in popover header with tooltip="Refresh available in a follow-on release" and onClick=no-op.</step>
    <step order="5">Build checkmark slot: onClick calls Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo({ pageType: "webresource", webresourceName: SMARTTODO_WEBRESOURCE_NAME, data: `regardingEntity=${entity}&amp;regardingId=${recordId}` }, LAYOUT_1_MODAL). Badge = todo count.</step>
    <step order="6">Build annotation slot: onClick calls Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo({ pageType: "webresource", webresourceName: NOTEPAD_WEBRESOURCE_NAME, data: `regardingEntity=${entity}&amp;regardingId=${recordId}` }, NOTEPAD_MODAL). Badge = memo count.</step>
    <step order="7">Return IHeaderToolbarProps with only enabled slots (respect enabled: {sparkle?, checkmark?, annotation?} — defaults all true).</step>
    <step order="8">Write tests: 3 slots emitted by default; enabled={sparkle:false} removes sparkle slot; checkmark handler invokes navigateTo with Layout 1; annotation handler invokes navigateTo with 70x80; refresh click is no-op.</step>
    <step order="9">Run tests.</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 012 ✅.</step>
    <step order="11">Document deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools><tool name="npm">Build + test</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/useRecordHeaderToolbarActions.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/__tests__/useRecordHeaderToolbarActions.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given default enabled, when hook runs, then IHeaderToolbarProps.iconSlots has 3 entries (sparkle, checkmark, annotation).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given enabled.sparkle=false, when hook runs, then iconSlots has 2 entries; sparkle is not present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">When sparkle onClick fires, then a Popover state opens; no Xrm.Navigation call is made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">When checkmark onClick fires, then Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo is called with pageType="webresource", webresourceName=SMARTTODO_WEBRESOURCE_NAME, and LAYOUT_1_MODAL options.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">When annotation onClick fires, then Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo is called with NOTEPAD_MODAL options.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Refresh icon click is a no-op in R1 (no navigateTo, no API call).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Sparkle popover UX (width, empty-state copy) is flagged as unresolved question U-03/U-04 in spec.md — pick sensible defaults ("maxWidth: 480px", empty-state: "No summary yet") and revisit in QA.</notes>

